    <statement><p>Simplify and write the following as a product of rational powers of <m>b</m> and <m>y</m>.</p>
<p>If <m>\displaystyle \frac{ \left(b^3 y^4\right)^{1/15}}
{b^{-1/3}y^{1/5}} = b^m y^n</m> then <m>m =</m> <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0001"/>  and <m>n =</m> <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>{\frac{8}{15}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>{\frac{1}{15}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p><m>\displaystyle{\begin{aligned}
   \amp \displaystyle \frac{ \left(b^3 y^4\right)^{1/15}}
{b^{-1/3}y^{1/5}} = 
   \frac{ b^{3/15} y^{4/15} }{b^{-1/3}  y^{1/5}} \\
   \amp = b^{(3/15+1/3)}y^{(4/15-1/5)}=b^{{{\frac{8}{15}}}}y^{{{\frac{1}{15}}}}\end{aligned}}</m></p>
</solution>
